          "title": "Daaluu",
          "subtitle": "Card game",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Daaluu is a Mongolian tile game family treated as its own tile family and modeled separately from western dominoes and khorol. Reference descriptions document dedicated daaluu tile compositions with zodiac and flower-style groups in regional variants."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Daaluu is documented in Mongolian regional tile play with dedicated tile compositions and profile-specific rules."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "2 to 8 players."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "One Daaluu 64 tile set."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Daaluu tiles and score tracking if the table profile uses cumulative scoring."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Tiles are distributed according to the active daaluu profile."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
